# 🚀 Elevator Controller Verification using UVM

## 📌 Overview
This project implements and verifies a Finite State Machine (FSM)-based elevator controller using SystemVerilog and UVM (Universal Verification Methodology).

The system simulates a basic elevator operating between floors 0 to 3, handling user requests and emergency conditions. A complete UVM testbench is used to validate the design with clean, event-driven output.

---

## 🧠 Features
- Supports 4 floors (0–3)
- Automatic movement (up/down)
- Door opens at destination floor
- Emergency mode (door opens immediately)
- Directed test sequence (predictable behavior)
- Clean output using event-based monitoring

---

## ⚙️ Design (FSM States)
- IDLE – Waiting for request  
- MOVE_UP – Elevator moves up  
- MOVE_DOWN – Elevator moves down  
- DOOR_OPEN – Door opens at target floor  
- EMERGENCY – Immediate door open  

---

## 🧪 UVM Architecture
- Sequence → Generates requests  
- Driver → Drives DUT inputs  
- Monitor → Observes outputs  
- Agent → Connects driver & sequencer  
- Environment → Contains agent  
- Test → Controls execution  

